-- CA_0172_la_city_by_district_batch_d1_2026.sql
-- LA-cities slice, by-district batch D1: five cities that elect their council BY DISTRICT but were modeled at large
-- (every council member on the whole-city polygon, so every address returned all of them and no district race could
-- be bound). Their DB rosters are complete and current, so this is a pure re-model + races:
--   * one LOCAL district row + X0001 polygon per council district (LA RR/CC precinct layer, Political_Boundaries/
--     MapServer/34, DST_CITY/DIV_CITY, dissolved; read 2026-09-23; QA: each city's districts cover its TIGER place
--     polygon 0.997-0.9996 with seam-only overlaps -- same method + positive control as CA_0141 / CA_0167);
--   * each sitting member's EXISTING office moves onto their district (term history moves with it), retitled
--     "Council Member (District N)". District assignment = each city's own council page, read 2026-09-22/23.
-- Inglewood's Mayor is elected at large and stays on its LOCAL_EXEC office. In Bellflower, Palmdale and West Covina the
-- council picks the mayor, so the member titled "Mayor" is simply that district's member.
-- SANTA CLARITA is mid-transition to districts: Ayala (D1) and Gibbs (D3) were elected by district in 2024; Weste,
-- McLean and Miranda hold at-large seats to Dec 2026 and stay on the whole-city office ("Council Member (At-Large)");
-- D2, D4 and D5 are first filled Nov 2026, so each gets a new office flagged vacant (no holder until then) carrying its
-- race -- the CA_0152 Montebello pattern. Weste runs in D4 as a sitting official, not as that seat's incumbent.
-- WEST COVINA also elects its City Clerk and City Treasurer; neither office existed, so both are created (Carson
-- pattern, on a new LOCAL_EXEC whole-city district) with holders Nickolas Lewis and Colleen B. Rozatti
-- (westcovina.gov/177/Elected-Officials).
--
-- CONTESTS (each clerk's list, verified name by name and district by district against the original):
--   Bellflower City Council District 1          2 candidate(s)  1 incumbent(s)
--   Inglewood Mayor                             6 candidate(s)  1 incumbent(s)
--   Inglewood City Council District 1           4 candidate(s)  0 incumbent(s)
--   Inglewood City Council District 2           2 candidate(s)  1 incumbent(s)
--   Palmdale City Council District 3            5 candidate(s)  1 incumbent(s)
--   Palmdale City Council District 4            4 candidate(s)  1 incumbent(s)
--   Palmdale City Council District 5            3 candidate(s)  0 incumbent(s)
--   West Covina City Council District 2         3 candidate(s)  1 incumbent(s)
--   West Covina City Council District 4         3 candidate(s)  1 incumbent(s)
--   West Covina City Council District 5         2 candidate(s)  1 incumbent(s)
--   West Covina City Clerk                      1 candidate(s)  1 incumbent(s)  (uncontested)
--   West Covina City Treasurer                  1 candidate(s)  1 incumbent(s)  (uncontested)
--   Santa Clarita City Council District 2       3 candidate(s)  0 incumbent(s)
--   Santa Clarita City Council District 4       5 candidate(s)  0 incumbent(s)
--   Santa Clarita City Council District 5       3 candidate(s)  0 incumbent(s)
-- Inglewood's Nov 3 election is its PRIMARY NOMINATING election: a candidate needs a majority, otherwise the top two
-- meet in a later runoff (the charter rule; the 2022 runoff was March 7 2023). Not on the ballot: Bellflower D3/D5
-- (appointed in lieu, EC 10229, 8/19/2026); Palmdale has no Mayor contest (council-chosen).
--
-- RACES go on '2026 LA County General' (d91a20ce-557e-4615-a31b-5b2b3df2ed14); primary_party NULL; no party stored.
-- IDEMPOTENT: fixed ids for every new row; office moves guarded on the target; every insert NOT EXISTS-guarded.

BEGIN;

